    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can offer personalized tutoring, breaking down complex topics in ways that suit different learning styles. They can provide immediate feedback and adapt to a student’s pace. In university settings, they can assist with problem-solving and even generate teaching materials. They’re not replacements for teachers, but as tools, they can supplement and enrich the learning experience."
